  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Late rallies keep working, and they worked again tonight.",
    "what_this_means": "This team doesn't need to lead early. Down three after three innings, they chased for four innings and caught it in the eighth when Lombard Jr. broke a tie with a home run. The game was close because they made it close. Nine runners left in scoring position but three of them mattered. The bullpen after Schlittler exited early didn't break. Fulmer, Hill, Gil, and Hanner combined for 5.1 scoreless innings. That's not survival. That's control. Two consecutive one-run wins now put them one game closer to Tampa Bay, and the pattern is becoming clear: they find ways to finish games that look finished. This only works until it doesn't.",
